From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:02:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdogb: skip the RPMh regulator readback

The bootloader on this device leaves the RPMh read channel unavailable to
Linux.  The regulator driver issues a read for every rail while it probes,
each read times out after ten seconds, and the abandoned request keeps the
TCS busy.  Every later RPMh transaction then fails as well, including the
BCM votes taken by the interconnect provider, and the boot stalls long
before the USB gadget shows up:

  qcom-rpmh-regulator 18200000.rsc:pm8150l-rpmh-regulators:
      failed to read voltage ret = -110
  qcom_icc_bcm_voter_commit -> icc_set_bw -> dwc3_qcom_probe
  Err: sending MMC RPMH requests (-110)

Set qcom,no-readback on the three PMIC regulator containers so the driver
uses the cached state instead of reading it back.

Signed-off-by: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@
 	pm8150-rpmh-regulators {
 		compatible = "qcom,pm8150-rpmh-regulators";
 		qcom,pmic-id = "a";
+		qcom,no-readback;
 
 		vdd-s1-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
 		vdd-s2-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
@@ -277,6 +278,7 @@
 	pm8150l-rpmh-regulators {
 		compatible = "qcom,pm8150l-rpmh-regulators";
 		qcom,pmic-id = "c";
+		qcom,no-readback;
 
 		vdd-s1-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
 		vdd-s2-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
@@ -390,6 +392,7 @@
 	pm8009-rpmh-regulators {
 		compatible = "qcom,pm8009-rpmh-regulators";
 		qcom,pmic-id = "f";
+		qcom,no-readback;
 
 		vdd-s1-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
 		vdd-s2-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
-- 
